.TH BROADCAST 1 "October 2026" "just3ws" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
broadcast \- direct, configure, and automate live video broadcasts across all three production archetypes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bin/broadcast
[\fB\-\-rewatch\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-errata\fR]
[\fB\-\-dialogue\fR]
[\fB\-\-cue\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIMODE\fR]
[\fB\-\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR]
[\fB\-\-subtitle\fR \fISUBTITLE\fR]
[\fB\-\-guest\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-citation\fR \fICITATION\fR]
[\fB\-\-prompt\fR \fIPROMPT\fR]
[\fB\-\-year\fR \fIYEAR\fR]
[\fB\-\-conference\fR \fICONF\fR]
[\fB\-\-status\fR]
[\fB\-\-list\fR]
[\fB\-\-validate\fR]
[\fB\-\-man\fR]
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B broadcast
is the unified broadcast director and orchestration engine for Mike Hall (Software Craftsmanship Signatory #106).
It manages live state across three distinct production archetypes, synchronizing HUD overlays in OBS Studio, YouTube scheduled metadata, and multi-track audio recording targets.
.PP
Every broadcast operates under strict craftsmanship constraints: zero em dashes, 1080p60 unscaled canvas resolution, Apple Silicon hardware encoding, and isolated application audio capture on macOS Golden Gate.
.SH BROADCAST ARCHETYPES
.TP
.B 1. Rewatch (\-\-rewatch <N>)
.I "The Sound Above: UGtastic Oral History Rewatch Series"
.br
A 31-episode curriculum reviewing over 200 UGtastic interviews (2009 to 2015) and the roots of the Chicago Software Craftsmanship movement.
Focuses on historical context, who inspired the interviewees before their keynotes, and what those practices teach us in the modern AI era.
.TP
.B 2. Errata (\-\-errata)
.I "Errata: Marginalia, Readings & Demonstrations"
.br
Solo broadcasts featuring book readings, concept breakdowns, live terminal workbench demonstrations, personal memoirs, and physical archival memorabilia showcases.
Modes include:
.B reading
(annotated book excerpts),
.B concept
(system cartography, cognitive load, architecture),
.B demo
(hands-on live coding, TDD cadence, sub-second feedback loops),
.B story
(first-person oral memoirs of early user groups), and
.B artifact
(physical badges, conference programs, and ephemera).
.TP
.B 3. Dialogue (\-\-dialogue)
.I "The Room: Invitational Conversations & Peer Inquiry"
.br
Invited guest discussions, collegial pair programming, and community roundtables exploring shared engineering history and technical craftsmanship.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rewatch " [" \fIEPISODE\fR "]"
Cue oral history rewatch episode from \fIobs/curation/sequence-manifest.json\fR (episodes 1 to 31).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-errata
Direct an Errata solo broadcast. Automatically switches overlays to Errata layout.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dialogue
Direct a Dialogue broadcast with invited peers or guests.
.TP
.BI \-\-cue " ID"
Cue a pre-configured topic from \fIobs/curation/errata-manifest.json\fR by ID (e.g. \fIerrata-concept-blink-test\fR).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Errata mode: \fBreading\fR, \fBconcept\fR, \fBdemo\fR, \fBstory\fR, or \fBartifact\fR.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title " " \fITITLE\fR
Set the broadcast topic, chapter heading, or essay title.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-subtitle " " \fISUBTITLE\fR
Set the contextual subtitle, role description, or book section.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-guest " " \fINAME\fR
Set interviewee or invited guest name.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-citation " " \fICITATION\fR
Set bibliographic citation, author credit, or physical archive provenance.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prompt " " \fIPROMPT\fR
Set the central philosophical question, book excerpt, or discussion thesis.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-year " " \fIYEAR\fR
Set historical year or artifact era (e.g. 2008, 2011).
.TP
.BI \-\-conference " CONF"
Set conference name, venue, or guest institutional affiliation.
.TP
.BI \-\-era " ERA"
Override historical era label.
.TP
.BI \-\-series " SERIES"
Override the series title banner displayed in OBS overlays.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Inspect active broadcast archetype, host, topic, and live overlay values.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Display the complete 31-episode rewatch catalog and pre-curated Errata entries.
.TP
.B \-\-validate
Run the automated OBS Studio setup, scene collection, and hardware contract test suite.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Display this manual page.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage summary and exit.
.SH OVERLAYS & LIVE SYNCHRONIZATION
When \fBbroadcast\fR updates the live state in \fIobs/overlays/overlay-state.json\fR, all browser source overlays in OBS Studio dynamically update within 2.5 seconds:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlower-third.html\fR: Renders guest credentials, citations, and core prompts.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnow-watching.html\fR: Displays the active topic badge, era tag, and live indicator.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstream-starting.html\fR: Pre-stream countdown and thematic quote carousel.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstream-outro.html\fR: Concluding credits and next episode preview.
.SH AUDIO ARCHITECTURE (MACOS GOLDEN GATE)
OBS Studio operates with 4-track isolated master recording:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTrack 1\fR: Composite stream mix (Mic + Application Audio + Overlays).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTrack 2\fR: Host microphone isolated with RNNoise suppression and compressor.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTrack 3\fR: Browser video playback isolated via ScreenCaptureKit (\fIsck_audio_capture\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTrack 4\fR: Remote guest audio isolated for post-production balancing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Check active broadcast status:
bin/broadcast --status

# List all curated episodes and errata items:
bin/broadcast --list

# Cue Episode 1 rewatch (Sergio Pereira):
bin/broadcast --rewatch 1

# Cue a pre-configured Errata concept broadcast:
bin/broadcast --cue errata-concept-blink-test

# Direct an ad-hoc live code refactoring demo:
bin/broadcast --errata --mode demo \\
  --title "Beck's Four Rules of Simple Design" \\
  --prompt "Refactoring legacy Ruby to intention-revealing code live."

# Direct an invited guest dialogue:
bin/broadcast --dialogue \\
  --guest "Corey Haines" \\
  --subtitle "Author, Understanding the 4 Rules of Simple Design" \\
  --title "Deliberate Practice in the Age of AI"

# Verify all OBS and audio contracts:
bin/broadcast --validate
.fi
.SH FILES
